--[[
STEAL A POTATO - map and kit builder (generated by tools/gen_build.py)

Runs unattended. Upload StealAPotato.fbx with Open Cloud, load it with
InsertService:LoadAsset and parent the result anywhere under Workspace, then run
this file with loadstring from the command-bar context. It:

  1. finds the imported MeshParts by name (inside the import that holds the four
     SAP_Axis marker cubes) and undoes any scale or turn the importer applied;
  2. keeps a clean copy of every mesh in ServerStorage.PotatoMeshes, so the script can
     be run again later even without a fresh import;
  3. builds Workspace.PotatoMap (Model) and ReplicatedStorage.PotatoKit (Folder):
     130 Parts, 685 MeshParts (285 different meshes), 14 markers,
     and the RootMonster's 109 keyframes in PotatoKit.RootAnimations;
  4. replaces the PotatoMap and PotatoKit an earlier run built, and deletes the
     import (only what this run brought in) and the marker cubes.

Safe to run twice. If the meshes can't be found it changes nothing and warns.
]]

